\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Kernel density estimates (Gaussian kernel, Scott bandwidth) over the gold set for the four controllers; dotted lines are medians and ticks are individual drawings ($n$ = 45 / 48 / 48 / 48 drawings, 71k / 76k / 76k / 76k pen-down samples for IK / streaming IK / ACT / SmolVLA). (a) Per-drawing path RMSE: the two learned policies separate cleanly from both IK variants. (b) Nearest-path error of every planned pen-down sample (densified plan): medians 0.256, 0.257, 0.141 and 0.120\,mm\xspace  . (c) Pen-down joint jerk: ACT has the lowest, SmolVLA between ACT and IK.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
